Writing Custom Solvers
Follow the built-in solver pattern to create a new analysis:
from mlsysim.hardware.types import HardwareNode

class PowerEfficiencyModel:
    def solve(self, hardware: HardwareNode) -&gt; dict:
        flops_per_watt = hardware.compute.peak_flops / hardware.tdp
        return {
            "device": hardware.name,
            "flops_per_watt": flops_per_watt.to("TFLOPs/s/kW"),
        }
See Writing a Custom Solver for the full guide.

Cite MLSys·im
Coursework, research, or infrastructure analysis that uses MLSys·im should cite it as shown below. The textbook has its own citation for work that draws on the book or the course materials.
